network-monitoring-selection is the vendor-neutral network monitoring and NMS DESIGN, monitoring-paradigm,
and platform-selection umbrella: which paradigm answers the question (SNMP polling for device health, flow
analytics for traffic, synthetic for user experience, packet capture for forensics), what the golden
signals are for a network, how to design alerts that get acted on, how monitoring scales across sites, and
which platform earns the deployment. It is the design-and-selection entry point for the NMS family;
per-vendor configuration and operations live in the sibling skills (prtg-network-monitoring,
kentik-network-monitoring land in PR 2 of this family; cacti-network-monitoring lands in PR 3).
Skill licensed MIT (the primary-source licence).

Scope + cadence (decided with the user at plan time, 2026-06-18 AskUserQuestion):
  - Naming = scope-explicit: umbrella `network-monitoring-selection` + `prtg-network-monitoring` +
    `kentik-network-monitoring` + `cacti-network-monitoring`.
  - PR cadence = three PRs: PR 1 = this umbrella; PR 2 = PRTG + Kentik (MIT single-source); PR 3 = Cacti
    (external, public-docs draft).
  - Vendor-skill scope = full ops (architecture + config + operations) per the DNS + Load-balancer
    precedent, since there are no pre-existing NMS diagnostic skills to route to.
  - This umbrella owns DESIGN / PARADIGM-CHOICE / PLATFORM-COMPARISON only; per-vendor configuration is
    routed out via "When not to use" to the three vendor skills.

